/** \page nml Namelist Reference

\tableofcontents

This section provides an overview of the namelists used in mHM for model configuration.
Each namelist is documented on a separate page, detailing its parameters and their usage.

\section nml_config Configuration Namelists

The configuration namelists define the model setup and runtime behavior.
They are all listed below, one page per namelist:

- \subpage config_project : Configuration for the overall project setup `&config_project`.
- \subpage config_domain : Configuration for model domains `&config_domain`.
- \subpage config_processes : Configuration for process case selection `&config_processes`.
- \subpage config_resolution : Configuration for model grid resolutions `&config_resolution`.
- \subpage config_optimize : Configuration for optimization settings `&config_optimize`.
- \subpage config_time : Configuration for time settings `&config_time`.
- \subpage config_input : Configuration for input data `&config_input`.
- \subpage config_coupling : Configuration for coupling settings `&config_coupling`.
- \subpage config_meteo : Configuration for meteorological component `&config_meteo`.
- \subpage config_mpr : Configuration for the multiscale parameter regionalization (MPR) `&config_mpr`.
- \subpage config_mhm : Configuration for the hydrological component `&config_mhm`.
- \subpage config_mrm : Configuration for the routing component (mRM) `&config_mrm`.
- \subpage config_observations : Configuration for reference observations `&config_observations`.

\section nml_parameters Parameter Namelists

Parameter namelists use the buffer-compatible `parameter_t` derived type in this fixed order:

`value, optimize, min, max`

These fields are used as follows:
- `value`: input value and initial calibration value.
- `optimize`: calibration switch (`.true.` = calibrate, `.false.` = keep fixed).
- `min`: minimum admissible parameter value.
- `max`: maximum admissible parameter value.

Bounds are supplied by each parameter schema, so fixed parameters can use `parameter = value`
and calibration with default bounds can use `parameter = value, .true.`. The complete form
`parameter = value, optimize, min, max` overrides those defaults.

They are all listed below, one page per namelist:

- \subpage interception_1 : Parameters for interception (case 1) `&interception_1`.
- \subpage snow_1 : Parameters for snow (case 1) `&snow_1`.
- \subpage soil_moisture_1 : Parameters for soil moisture (case 1) `&soil_moisture_1`.
- \subpage soil_moisture_2 : Parameters for soil moisture (case 2) `&soil_moisture_2`.
- \subpage soil_moisture_3 : Parameters for soil moisture (case 3) `&soil_moisture_3`.
- \subpage soil_moisture_4 : Parameters for soil moisture (case 4) `&soil_moisture_4`.
- \subpage direct_runoff_1 : Parameters for direct runoff (case 1) `&direct_runoff_1`.
- \subpage pet_m2 : Parameters for PET (case -2 - aspect correction) `&pet_m2`.
- \subpage pet_m1 : Parameters for PET (case -1 - LAI correction) `&pet_m1`.
- \subpage pet_1 : Parameters for PET (case 1 - Hargreaves-Samani) `&pet_1`.
- \subpage pet_2 : Parameters for PET (case 2 - Priestley-Taylor) `&pet_2`.
- \subpage pet_3 : Parameters for PET (case 3 - Penman-Monteith) `&pet_3`.
- \subpage interflow_1 : Parameters for interflow (case 1) `&interflow_1`.
- \subpage percolation_1 : Parameters for percolation (case 1) `&percolation_1`.
- \subpage routing_1 : Parameters for routing (case 1 - Muskingum) `&routing_1`.
- \subpage routing_2 : Parameters for routing (case 2 - adaptive timestep) `&routing_2`.
- \subpage routing_3 : Parameters for routing (case 3 - varying celerity) `&routing_3`.
- \subpage neutrons_1 : Parameters for neutrons (case 1 - Desilets) `&neutrons_1`.
- \subpage neutrons_2 : Parameters for neutrons (case 2 - COSMIC) `&neutrons_2`.
- \subpage baseflow_1 : Parameters for geological baseflow recession (case 1) `&baseflow_1`.
- \subpage river_temperature_1 : Parameters for river temperature (case 1) `&river_temperature_1`.

\section nml_outputs Output Namelists

The output namelists define which model outputs are generated during simulation.
They are all listed below, one page per namelist:

- \subpage output_mhm : Output configuration for mHM `&output_mhm`.
- \subpage output_mrm : Output configuration for mRM `&output_mrm`.

*/
